A||||9||Scott2M4||Trunk carpet needs work||||5||
Z||000000||Scott2M4||12-01-1999||08:30 AM||||The previous owner of my 87SC5 liked to keep leaky brake fluid containers in the trunk of the car.  Now, I have a brake fluid pond in there.<P>Can the carpet be cleaned of this crap?  How about replaced - can you purchase trunk carpet sections like you can interior carpet sections?||||reg||5
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||12-01-1999||08:44 AM||||Scott, It will be difficult to find a new trunk carpet. I would take it out and pressure wash it with whatever detergent you want. That should cure your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||12-01-1999||09:06 AM||||Just replace it...go down to your local parts store and buy replacement carpet and use the old carpet as a template for cutting the new.<P>Another option is a local home center which may have remnants or outdoor carpet in a color that may approximate or match what you have now. I found gray material that exactly matched my trunk carpet at my local Menards (Midwest home center chain). Used an X-Acto knife and scissors to cut it.<P>If it's only the bottom that's bad, just cut a piece to cover that. ||||reg||10
Z||000003||fieroshop||12-01-1999||09:45 AM||||That carpet will never get cleaned enough and you will always have residue there. One of the things we do at my shop is go to the wreckers and find one in decent shape and then we steam clean that one and it looks like new. It is also cheaper. I've got several trunk-mats in stock just for that reason||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-01-1999||12:08 PM||||This is off topic, but it made me laugh. A couple years ago, back in high school, our class took a trip to the mall of America. While on the highway one of the guys saw a Menards(never heard of them before) in a town we were passing through.   As he pointed to the store we all burst out laughing at the name. I know I know, childish humor, but I think I will always remember that spot in the trip the most.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dogtired||12-01-1999||01:34 PM||||OK Menards? (guess you had to be there)??<BR>86GT trunk carpet not bad 87SE a little worse for wear. So for the last 10 years plus the trunk makes a great work bench when working on those greasy parts??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Saw an 84 yesterday that had a black carpet in the trunk. In all my other Fiero's it has been that gray?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Maybe black was a replacement?||||reg||6
Z||000006||ChadMan||12-01-1999||02:33 PM||||I think black trunk carpet was factory equipment on non-SE 84's.  My 84 was a base (but not econo) model and it had black carpet, and a buddy with another base 84 had the black carpet too.<P>Strangely enough, my 84 was loaded EXCEPT for the SE package, so I had all kinds of power stuff, air and cruise, but 13" steel wheels and no WS6 suspension.  What a gyp.||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||12-01-1999||03:01 PM||||You can laugh, but Menards beats all the other home improvement chains hands down on selection and price. John Menard is also big into racing...his Indy car was on the pole position in 1997 and 1998 at the 500.<P>Oops, better cool it with the Menards spamming...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||12-02-1999||01:10 AM||||Class trip to the Mall of America?  doesn't sound like that much fun... I may be a little bit jaded, though, since I live about 20 minutes away from the place...||||reg||12
Z||000009||fiero56||12-02-1999||08:30 AM||||We actually went to tour some colleges out there, but they were so boring that all we remember is the mall. Pretty sad the mall was the highlight of the trip.  But it wa nice getting out of a week of school for it.  <BR>This was before I had my Fiero, or I would have been pretty antsy to get back home and drive it. I can't believe I've gone this far without getting "the fever". Probably because it's pretty cold here right now.||||reg||1
